# The per-crate outside-dependency allowlist (R11.12).
#
# R11.12 forbids a dependency on anything outside the ten phinet crates and
# "the published crates.io dependencies already in use". Already in use is a
# per-crate fact, not a workspace-wide one: phiano carries a server and a
# parser, the lower crates carry five crates between them, and a list shared
# across the ten would either fail phiano's axum or wave through phistd's.
# So the allowlist is per crate, read from the ten manifests and pinned here.
#
# Read at the commit that landed task 2.1 of the 64-operators spec, from the
# union of each crate's [dependencies] and [dev-dependencies].
#
# One line per crate: `<crate> = <dep>, <dep>, ...`, deps sorted, an empty
# right-hand side meaning the crate declares no outside dependency at all.
# A novel outside dependency fails the Structure_Check until it is recorded
# here, and a re-recording writes the previous list, the new list and the
# stated reason (R11.10).

phistd = num-complex, rayon, serde
phifno = bincode, serde
phiton = bincode, serde, serde_json
phical = num-complex, serde, serde_json
phiecs = bincode, rayon, serde, serde_json
phiclm =
phient = bincode, proc-macro2, rayon, reqwest, serde, serde_json, syn
philog = serde
phisor =
phiano = axum, bincode, num-complex, proc-macro2, rayon, reqwest, rustyline, serde, serde_json, syn, tokio, tokio-stream, tower-http

# The frozen operand set's fingerprint (R7.6): `phistd::mix64` folded byte by
# byte over `phinet/crates/phical/tests/keyboard/operands.tsv`, carriage
# returns dropped so a CRLF checkout holds the same record. The set is the
# whole input to the agreement check and was written before the first
# agreement run, so a modification of it must fail the run rather than
# quietly change what was agreed. Pinned here, beside the other thing this
# file pins: a fact about a file read once and held to.
#
# It is a comment line because the right-hand sides above are dependency
# lists and `the_allowlist_golden_is_the_manifests_true_outside_state` holds
# the keys to the ten crates; the fingerprint is not a crate and must not
# become one. `frozen::the_set_is_the_fingerprint_pinned_in_the_golden_record`
# reads it from here.
#
# A re-recording writes the previous fingerprint, the new one and the stated
# reason (R11.10).
#
# frozen-operands = 0xa7f3c7189e923483
